4. Gao frontend: integration and startup

Use Python 3.10+ with Tkinter, from the repository root:

  python3 main.py --gui

The existing main.py calls gui_gao.main(). Register on first use. No teammate entry-point changes are needed.

For an isolated demonstration:

  python3 -m gui_gao --demo

On macOS, open gui_gao/launch_demo.command. The old launcher path remains a small compatibility shortcut. The obsolete .app wrapper is not included. Demo credentials are gao_demo / Campus123, with fictional users/items in a temporary directory that is removed on normal exit.

The 10 November English version integrates with upstream 7ef1a95. Pages, prompts, sample content, comments and frontend documentation are English. Display labels map to the current books/electronics/clothing/household and on_sale/off_sale enums. User-authored text is preserved; data is not migrated.

Connected pages include sign-in/registration, browse/search/sort/pagination, details, publish/edit, own listings, account settings, saved items, public comments, enquiries and activity. Design B's illustrations, live previews, image zoom, checklist interactions and controllable route/clock animations are retained.

Feature services execute their actual business methods. Gao's local adapter binds validation to the selected user/item services so demo/practice directories remain isolated. It normalizes favorite results without editing feature_du. Unavailable saved items are read-only history because the current service rejects all favorite toggles for off-sale/deleted items. Enquiries support creation/query only; no payment/accept/cancel actions are added. See gui_gao/HANDOFF.md for service-context injection and query handoff needs.

The standalone web design prototype remains separate and is not a production backend entry point or part of this upload. Runtime JSON, caches and obsolete wrappers are excluded.

